<h2 id="orgebfa827"><span class="section-number-2">7.</span> Key Concept Illustration</h2>
<div class="outline-text-2" id="text-7">
</div>
<div id="outline-container-org26569ed" class="outline-3">
<h3 id="org26569ed"><span class="section-number-3">7.1.</span> Sliding Window Median</h3>
<div class="outline-text-3" id="text-7-1">
<ol class="org-ol">
<li><b><b>Create Two Heaps</b></b>:
<ul class="org-ul">
<li>Max heap for the lower half of the window.</li>
<li>Min heap for the upper half.</li>
</ul></li>
<li><b><b>Window Slide</b></b>:
<ul class="org-ul">
<li>As the window moves, add new elements to the heaps.</li>
<li>Rebalance heaps to ensure size condition (max heap has at most one extra element).</li>
</ul></li>
<li><b><b>Calculate Median</b></b>:
<ul class="org-ul">
<li>If heaps are of equal size, median is the average of the top elements.</li>
<li>If max heap has more elements, the median is the top element of the max heap.</li>
</ul></li>
</ol>

<p>
Example:
</p>
<ul class="org-ul">
<li>Array: `[1, 3, 5, 7, 2]`, Window size: `3`</li>
<li>Resulting medians: `[1, 2, 3]`</li>
</ul>
</div>
